WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.420
Vines, branches, and tendrils grab at&nbsp;
682’s wriggling body, as the skinless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.960
grinning face of the Skeleton Queen bears&nbsp;
down. She is in total control. For one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:19.140
the first times ever, 682 has encountered a&nbsp;
threat who might be too powerful for even its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:25.740
strength and adaptability to surpass. How could&nbsp;
such an impossible circumstance come to pass?

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.860
Lost in an endless abyss of liminal realities,&nbsp;
separated from its closest companions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:37.020
and officially declared to be neutralized&nbsp;
by The SCP Foundation, the immortal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:44.100
reptilian entity known as 682 continues its&nbsp;
incomprehensible journey through The Backrooms.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:50.400
682 had explored over twenty different levels of&nbsp;
the Backrooms, from vast oceans, to lost cities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.520
to even mind-warping spaces that evoked distant&nbsp;
childhood memories. Very little, if any,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:04.500
of what 682 had encountered could be described as&nbsp;
fun or adventurous. In 682’s mind, The Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.660
was a nightmare controlled by malicious forces&nbsp;
that only wanted to bring harm to the creature.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:15.120
The lizard had faced scores of violent entities&nbsp;
ranging from low-level fodder like clumps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:21.120
smilers, and death moths, spear-wielding&nbsp;
mini-bosses like Tiny and Argus, and one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.100
particularly crafty and well-equipped elderly&nbsp;
explorer. Through all of these encounters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:32.700
the dimension-hopping hijinks that came with&nbsp;
them, 682 had become enduring and resilient.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:39.360
The uncontrollable rage and disgust for life that&nbsp;
had defined 682’s personality during its time in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:46.860
containment had gradually subsided into an almost&nbsp;
enlightened state of determination. The will to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:52.620
its own master, decide its own destiny, and&nbsp;
to travel The Backrooms not as a conqueror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.800
but as an entity seeking freedom for its sake.
It spent a long time contemplating its purpose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.500
in the cryptic ruins of the petrified garden on&nbsp;
level 23 before making a new effort to travel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.260
between layers of the backrooms. As one might&nbsp;
expect, the next level that 682 was able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:17.640
access was Level 24, known by some as The Study,&nbsp;
but better known by its locals as The Moon.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:24.960
Even as far as levels in the Backrooms go,&nbsp;
level 24 was an unusual concept for 682 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.300
understand at first. The walkable portion of the&nbsp;
level appeared to be a plastic model of a moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:36.240
blown up to colossal proportions. The moon&nbsp;
was part of a scale model of the solar system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:43.020
and was situated inside a Victorian-era&nbsp;
study of impossible size. The exact details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.520
of the massive room were hard to see,&nbsp;
given the anomalous blurry filter that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.420
appeared to impede the vision of those&nbsp;
who tried to look away from the moon.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.860
“Hmm… no consistent theme with the previous&nbsp;
levels, vague and inexplicable properties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:08.160
and a seemingly random resemblance to human-made&nbsp;
structures. Classic backrooms,” 682 mused.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:14.580
In the distant expanse of the study, Entity&nbsp;
682 thought that it saw a titanic human man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:20.640
in a tuxedo pulling a book from one of the shelves&nbsp;
and sitting down to read it. This blurry giant was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.640
known simply as “Beuford” and he was the only&nbsp;
unique entity to this level of the Backrooms.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.320
The craters and rifts of the moon were&nbsp;
home to swarms of death moths and clumps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:35.520
though there were noticeably not as many&nbsp;
of these hostile entities as on prior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:41.280
levels. 682 regarded the presence of these&nbsp;
familiar foes as something of a novelty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.260
given the amount of time it had spent&nbsp;
on the relatively safe level 23.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:52.080
The more things change, the more&nbsp;
they stay just as disgusting.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:57.720
While 682 was not exactly pleased with having to&nbsp;
share the same reality as these infernal things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.680
it was not about to rush in&nbsp;
and start taking names. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:06.060
the researchers at the Foundation could&nbsp;
see SCP-682 now, they might assume that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:11.460
the reptile had been reformed of its&nbsp;
violent ways. This was not the case.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:18.900
682 had come to accept that these creatures had no&nbsp;
real ecosystem or drive to propagate themselves as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:24.300
other life did. The mechanics of their existence&nbsp;
seemed to be limited to the mere fact that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:30.720
were extensions of the Backrooms itself: obstacles&nbsp;
placed in the path of explorers to thwart their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:37.020
progress. They were more like the enemies of&nbsp;
a video game than sentient lifeforms, and 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.600
had come to believe that fighting them would be&nbsp;
doing exactly what the Backrooms wanted it to do.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:48.480
If 682 needed to defend itself, it would&nbsp;
absolutely fight back against these stock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.540
entities, but by now, it was obvious that they&nbsp;
were not a real threat. There were better games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.540 --> 00:05:00.780
to play in the arcade of life, and 682 was&nbsp;
not feeling particularly flush with tokens.&nbsp;

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:07.080
Appropriately enough, the next level that&nbsp;
682 arrived at - level 25 - was filled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.240
a wide selection of arcade machines.&nbsp;
Once again, the Backrooms had thrown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.940
another devious curve ball in the direction of&nbsp;
682. The hard to destroy reptile was reminded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:23.220
once again of just how unpredictable the&nbsp;
variations in theme could be between levels.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:29.880
True to its retro aesthetic, Level 25 seemed to&nbsp;
be covered in a thin layer of dust. The arcade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:35.280
machines themselves were damaged and broken&nbsp;
down. The few that did seem functional were not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:42.360
equipped with any game that 682 was familiar with.&nbsp;
Then again, 682 was not exactly an avid gamer.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:47.040
Perhaps the sorry state of the arcade would&nbsp;
be explained by the level being where the 80s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.280
went to die or, more likely, by the fact no human&nbsp;
explorer had made it this far into the Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:59.340
in quite some time. The lack of humans in an&nbsp;
environment designed for them was hardly a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:05.160
occurrence inside of the Backrooms, and as usual,&nbsp;
the general idea seemed to be that something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:11.520
was usually normal, like a hotel or an office,&nbsp;
presented in a way that made it inconvenient.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.980
An arcade where no games could be played was&nbsp;
certainly a bummer, but considering that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:21.360
several layers farther down than a level where&nbsp;
explorers were forced to confront their traumatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.340
pasts, and another level that threatened all&nbsp;
explorers with evershifting extreme environments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:31.680
the plight of being stuck in a defunct&nbsp;
arcade was a bit of an underwhelming concept.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:38.100
682 had long since accepted that there was no&nbsp;
linear difficulty curve to the Backrooms, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:44.280
given that this place was also devoid of entities,&nbsp;
Level 25 didn’t seem to have much to offer the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:51.060
reptile. With no other options, 682 decided to try&nbsp;
one of the arcade machines. Naturally, it didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:57.240
carry any quarters on its being, but that was only&nbsp;
a minor quibble to a creature as adaptable as 682.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.220
I can do anything.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:05.400
As 682 approached one of the functional arcade&nbsp;
machines, it developed a quarter-shaped skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:10.740
tag on the tip of its snout, similar to the&nbsp;
knobby growth of a male gharial crocodile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:16.260
It extended this growth towards the coin&nbsp;
slot on a wire-thin appendage. As if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:21.660
were an actual quarter, 682 did its best&nbsp;
impression of placing a quarter inside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:27.780
an arcade machine. Once the machine blinked&nbsp;
to life, 682 retracted its organic quarter.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:31.740
The bright screen of the cabinet began&nbsp;
to shuffle rapidly through numbers like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:37.680
a slot machine. It did this for several minutes&nbsp;
until landing on the number 28. Sparks of energy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:44.340
coursed through the arcade cabinet, and a sudden&nbsp;
burst of light whisked 682 several levels ahead.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:49.920
682 could see a tunnel of light on all sides&nbsp;
as it flew through the liminal space between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.800
liminal spaces. It was able to perceive a hint&nbsp;
of level 26 - a seemingly ordinary apartment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:02.220
building - and level 27 - an innocent looking&nbsp;
hot spring inside of a cave. Both concepts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:08.040
were old hat at this point, so 682 didn’t&nbsp;
feel too bad about skipping them. Besides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:13.860
it was a free being now, and what was freer than&nbsp;
breaking the rules and skipping a few levels?

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:17.580
Unless the Backrooms were hoping it would do that?&nbsp;

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:22.380
But there was no time to think about the&nbsp;
inscrutable intentions of the abyss’ creators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:29.520
because 682 had reached the other side of the&nbsp;
light tunnel and been deposited into level 28 - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:35.760
dimension with a navy blue sky and a single&nbsp;
large castle on the hill - the only landmark.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:41.700
682 moved towards the castle and was greeted by&nbsp;
the sound of a great thunder above. Dark storm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:46.680
clouds began to fill the sky as rain poured&nbsp;
down onto the forested valley surrounding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:52.440
keep. While no ordinary storm would deter a&nbsp;
being as powerful as 682, the howling winds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:56.760
and flashes of lightning signaled that&nbsp;
this weather was anything but ordinary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.500
The reptile naturally decided to continue&nbsp;
into the only available shelter - the castle.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:05.400
It barged in through one of the walls&nbsp;
in an effort to hide itself from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:09.600
elements. It soon learned that it&nbsp;
was not alone. A foreboding figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:14.820
approached from the darkness of the keep,&nbsp;
clad head to toe in colorful blue armor.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.360
“Who goes there? Answer me, you scaly knave!”

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:23.280
Feeling a bit spicy, 682 decided to&nbsp;
break out an old favorite threat:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.860
“What good does it do for a lamb to&nbsp;
know the name of its butcher? I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:34.440
simply passing through. You’re just one more&nbsp;
lifeless husk dreamed up by the Backrooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:40.380
so leave me be and return to your&nbsp;
dull routine of scaring weak humans.”

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:46.380
“Foul beast!” The Blue Knight said. “I&nbsp;
would never scare humans on purpose. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.720
happen to quite respect them. As a matter of fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.100
I have met a particularly good human&nbsp;
who taught me so many wonderful things.”

00:09:53.100 --> 00:10:00.540
“You say you’ve met a good human?” 682&nbsp;
asked. “Other than the exception of the dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:06.300
I can’t think of any humans that are&nbsp;
worthy of existence, let alone ‘good.’”

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:09.540
“Well then, you don’t know&nbsp;
Sarah!” The Blue Knight said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.900
seemingly in a state of rising emotional distress.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:18.180
The storm outside began to grow in intensity&nbsp;
in response to the Blue Knight’s provoked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:24.540
reaction. 682 found this somewhat intriguing and&nbsp;
decided to push the armored figure a bit further.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:29.280
“Is she your girlfriend?” 682 taunted.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:35.460
682 was becoming simultaneously more amused and&nbsp;
disgusted by this Blue Knight as the interaction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:41.040
went on. It was clear that the Blue Knight was&nbsp;
a bit of a lunatic and definitely a soft-hearted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:47.400
being, though as 682 pondered his words, an odd&nbsp;
feeling of realization washed over the reptile.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:54.540
Was the current situation regarding 682’s lost&nbsp;
traveling companion - Entity 7 Jerry - not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:59.100
dissimilar from what the knight was going&nbsp;
through in regards to this human named Sarah?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:04.920
682 had learned much about the Backrooms during&nbsp;
his time traveling with the blue hyacinth macaw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:10.800
and did miss the avian entity very much. The&nbsp;
idea that Jerry may have forgotten about 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:16.080
and might be on adventures somewhere&nbsp;
else made 682 almost feel regretful.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:22.740
Suddenly, tormenting this overly sensitive knight&nbsp;
didn’t seem to be that much fun to 682. All at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:28.080
once, the reptile wanted out of this level,&nbsp;
so he ordered the night to give him an exit.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:32.460
The blue knight shook its head for a&nbsp;
bit, but ultimately relented. He led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:38.220
682 to an archway deep in the castle made&nbsp;
of solid bones. It was a dimensional portal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:43.320
like many of those seen in the Backrooms,&nbsp;
and it was carved with the number 32.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:48.840
“This portal shall take you to the Forest&nbsp;
of the Skeleton Queen on level 32. It is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:53.880
a dangerous place where you will almost&nbsp;
certainly meet your demise. The Skeleton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:59.220
Queen is not known for her hospitality.”
The Forest of the Skeleton Queen was about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:05.100
what one might expect from its name. A dark&nbsp;
and gloomy woodland beneath a starless sky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:10.680
and a crescent moon. Of course, there were also&nbsp;
the countless skeletons floating among the trees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.700
to give the level some personality.&nbsp;
All of them seemed somewhat alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:19.560
but like many of the Backrooms other&nbsp;
tricks, this may have only been an illusion.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.820
It’ll do.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:27.300
Before 682 could even fully take in the scenery,&nbsp;
it could see another entity moving between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:33.060
trees. It appeared to be a human woman in a&nbsp;
Victorian dress and skeletal face paint. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:38.160
appeared to gesture to 682, beckoning the&nbsp;
reptile into the forest. There was nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:43.620
to lose yet, so 682 took the mysterious&nbsp;
woman’s provocation and followed her.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:49.680
Not too far down the path, 682 lost sight&nbsp;
of this strange human woman. It was as if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:54.840
she had been there a moment and was gone&nbsp;
the next. 682 pondered the odd nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.620
this encounter and decided to turn back&nbsp;
around and follow a different path.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:03.840
As soon as 682 turned, the woman appeared&nbsp;
before the reptile again, but this time her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:09.240
overall form was a lot more sinister. She&nbsp;
was tall and gaunt, with hardly any skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:16.140
and the white of her bones shone ominously in the&nbsp;
moonlight. She smiled an evil smile, and without a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:22.860
single word, she snapped her fingers - causing&nbsp;
the entire forest to immediately turn on 682.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:29.520
It was an attack more sudden and more complete&nbsp;
than any 682 had ever experienced. There was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:34.680
no chance to sense her hostility, no&nbsp;
room to adapt or to react. The trees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:40.500
took hold of 682 and in a display of immense&nbsp;
supernatural power that defied all logic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:48.000
tore 682’s very spirit out of its physical form&nbsp;
and dragged into the darkness beneath the forest.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:53.820
In its long and miserable life, the immortal&nbsp;
reptile 682 had endured every punishment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.820 --> 00:14:00.120
and form of damage in creation, but here and&nbsp;
now in the Backrooms, for the very first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:06.480
682 would not have the luxury of its hard&nbsp;
to destroy infinitely adaptable body. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:12.840
now a helpless, disembodied soul without any&nbsp;
means to defend itself, the perfect plaything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.120
for the Skeleton Queen herself. Has the&nbsp;
unkillable reptile truly been killed?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.660
Now check out “Could SCP-682 be Contained in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:22.860
Backrooms?” and “SCP-682 Makes&nbsp;
Friends in BACKROOMS” for more!

